Subject: [SE3-P9] winedmo: ignore empty input samples

An empty input sample left the transform's AVPacket empty, and FFmpeg takes
an empty packet as the end of the stream. In VRChat, AVPro's audio effect
answers DRAIN with one empty sample. The resampler after it then returned
MF_E_END_OF_STREAM instead of asking for more input, the session stopped
pulling that branch, and the audio renderer never got its end marker: every
video stopped at its end while the audio ran dry.

An empty sample carries no data, so accept it and send nothing. Draining has
its own request, so no caller relies on an empty push.

---
diff --git a/dlls/winedmo/unix_transform.c b/dlls/winedmo/unix_transform.c
--- a/dlls/winedmo/unix_transform.c
+++ b/dlls/winedmo/unix_transform.c
@@ -1088,6 +1088,10 @@
         return STATUS_SUCCESS;
     }
 
+    /* An empty sample carries no data, and an empty AVPacket would tell FFmpeg
+     * that the stream ended. Draining has its own request (transform_drain). */
+    if (!params->size) return STATUS_SUCCESS;
+
     if (t->drain_requested || t->draining) return STATUS_DEVICE_BUSY;
 
     if (!t->is_audio)
